--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY MAPPING (web → Apple)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web source is a PURE PRESENTATIONAL primitive (no data hooks, no charts, no maps).
It has exactly two top-level render branches, faithfully reproduced:
  1. cells.length === 0      → empty state (web `<EmptyState message icon/>`)
  2. otherwise               → responsive grid of tinted status cells
Per-cell variants reproduced in full: the 5 statuses (ok/warning/error/inactive/
unknown), `compact` (value hidden + tighter padding + forced 2 cols), and the 2/3/4
column responsive collapse (web container-query `containerColsClass`).

The generic prompt's data-driven states (loading/error/stale/offline) DO NOT EXIST in
this source — they belong to the DATA-BOUND widgets that COMPOSE this primitive (e.g.
SecurityStatusWidget renders skeleton/error then hands resolved `cells` to the grid).
Reproducing them here would be fabricated drift; honoring "reproduce the branches that
exist in the web source" is the faithful reading. Every branch that exists is rendered
— never a blank box (empty → friendly TSEmptyState; content → the grid).

  web EmptyState (@/components/feedback)  → TSEmptyState (ContentUnavailableView)   [native counterpart]
  web statusStyles (emerald/amber/red…)   → WidgetCellStatus.tone → TSTone (P1/S9)
  web container queries (@xs=320,@sm=384)  → WidgetStatusGridLayout.columnCount(width)
  web StatusCell.icon (ReactNode)          → systemImage (SF Symbol name)
  web text-xs / text-sm                    → Font.TS.caption / Font.TS.body
  web min-h-[44px], size-2 dot, /10 //20   → minHeight 44, 8pt dot, opacity .10/.20
  Tailwind classes                         → P1/S9 tokens (TSSpacing/TSRadius/Color.TS)
  t(key, default)                          → WidgetStatusGridStrings facade (P1/S10)
  (none)                                   → P1/S11 `view.opened` telemetry, slug "WidgetStatusGrid"

